  'macon-towing-guide': {
    longTitle: "Macon Towing Guide | Tips, Laws & How to Choose | All Hours Towing | (478) 500-8118",
    subtitle: "Everything you need to know about towing in Macon, GA — from laws to choosing a company.",
    longDescription: `Choosing a towing company in Macon, Georgia isn't something most drivers think about until they're standing on the side of the road with a dead vehicle. This guide from All Hours Towing Macon GA helps you understand what to look for before an emergency happens, and what to know when you need a tow right now. First, understand Georgia's towing laws: under the Georgia Move Over Law, drivers must move over one lane when approaching any stationary vehicle displaying flashing lights—including tow trucks. Our operators appreciate when motorists give them space to work safely. Second, know your rights: in Georgia, you have the right to choose which towing company handles your vehicle unless law enforcement specifically directs otherwise. You're never required to use a company simply because they arrived first or were called by a third party. When selecting a towing company in Macon, look for these indicators of reliability: local physical address, insurance and licensing, transparent pricing, 24/7 availability with live dispatchers, and fleet quality. For insurance purposes, document the before-and-after condition of your vehicle with photos before it's loaded onto a tow truck. Keep the tow company's invoice for reimbursement. If you're in an accident, our accident recovery team can coordinate directly with your insurance carrier. Understanding Macon's local geography helps too: I-75 is the main north-south artery with heavy truck traffic; I-16 connects Macon to Savannah; I-475 is the western bypass useful for avoiding downtown congestion. Knowing your nearest cross streets or the closest exit number helps our dispatcher pinpoint your location instantly. Save our number (478) 500-8118 in your phone now—when you need a tow, you'll be glad you did.`,
